# Features: each detection in a folder of its own (Features/<Name>/), which
# registers itself into the registries of Core/ and UI/ above, so it loads
# after them: Kind, Data (its static tables), Text, Mark, Slip or Card,
# then Capture. Its Dev.lua goes in the block at the foot
# (.claude/skills/new-feature/folder.md). Level-ups,
# Trade, then Chat come first: their Dev.lua write at the same points of
# Tester's script, a session's level-ups before its trade, a trade before
# the whispers about it, and Tester's first session's whispers before the
# campfire's row. Deaths, Close calls, then Witnesses: Close calls wear
# Deaths' card (registered at load), the witnesses chart a rescue as a
# close call's card does; their Dev.lua write at "route" in that order.
# Hunts after Close calls: both lists give CreatureNames.Of creatures'
# names, read in the order they registered (close calls' first, as before).
# Firsts before
# Profession caps: both take their first reading on SD_WORLD_SETTLED, the
# bags' first, as when they were one of Capture/Journey.lua's timers.
# Duels anywhere in the block: the client events it hears are its own, and
# the two messages it fires are heard by core first (ns.Duelling).
Features/LevelUps/Kind.lua
Features/LevelUps/Capture.lua
Features/Trade/Kind.lua
Features/Trade/Capture.lua
Features/Chat/Kind.lua
Features/Chat/Capture.lua
Features/Campfire/Kind.lua
