# Hunts' capture stays where it always was, after Capture/: it
# shares the quest events, the kills, the loot window and the login with
# Capture/, so every event order stays the old one
# (Features/Hunts/Capture.lua's header).
Features/Hunts/Capture.lua
# Witnesses' capture stays where its file was, after Capture/: it reads the
# same units as Capture/Nearby.lua's reunion toast and must still run after
# it, as on every event it shares with Capture/
# (Features/Witnesses/Capture.lua's header).
Features/Witnesses/Capture.lua

#@do-not-package@
# Development tooling: diagnostics, /sd art, /sd journey and /sd testdata. They
# register their own /sd commands. The packager strips this block, so a
# release never loads them (.pkgmeta leaves the folder out as well, and
# every Features/*/Dev.lua). A feature's Dev.lua adds its test data to
# /sd testdata (TestData.Register), so it comes after Dev/TestData.lua.
Dev/Art.lua
Dev/Diagnostics.lua
Dev/LootProbe.lua
Dev/HandTest.lua
Dev/SightingsDebug.lua
Dev/JourneyDebug.lua
Dev/TestData.lua
